/* book exam traps: ppm is parts per million, not millimetres per metre. 3 ppm is 3 mm per km, not 3 mm per m. | Add the constant part and the ppm part after scaling. Do not multiply 3 ppm by the constant 3 mm. | The prism constant has a sign and differs by prism type. A wrong value shifts every distance by the same amount. | EDM measures slope distance. Without a vertical angle reduction it is not horizontal distance. | Reflectorless mode is short-range and surface-dependent; it does not remove atmospheric correction or give the same accuracy as a prism. */
